


OS/8  STARTUP.				11/29/74. LM (12/19/74)
*************

1. TURN ON ALL POWER SWITCHES. COMPUTER, CRT AND INTERFACE
   ON. TELETYPE ON LINE.

2. MOUNT TAPES. CONSULT PROGRAM WRITEUP FOR TAPE
   NAMES AND UNITS.

	<---	WRITE ENABLED	REMOTE	--->
	=====	=====		=====	=====
	I   I	I   I		I   I	I   I
	I---I	I---I	    OFF I---I	I---I
	I(1)I	I(2)I		I(3)I	I(4)I
	=====	=====		=====	=====
	FORWARD	WRITE LOCK	LOCAL	REVERSE
    TAPE-MOTION				TAPE-MOTION

  A) PUT TAPE ON REEL, WRAP TAPE ONTO THE TAKEUP REEL.
  B) FLIP SWITCH (3) ON "LOCAL".
  C) PUSH FORWARD TAPE MOTION BUTTON (1) FOR A FEW SECONDS.
  D) FLIP SWITCH (3) TO "REMOTE".
  E) UNLESS REQUESTED IN THE PROGRAM WRITEUP,
     SWITCH (2) SHOULD BE ON "WRITE ENABLED".

3. SET ALL SWITCHES ON PANNEL TO ZERO (SLANTING TOWARD CRT)
   EXCEPT ONES MARKED "DEADSTART".

   PRESS IN ORDER  1) I/O PRESET
		   2) DO
			(WAIT FOR TAPE MOTION TO STOP)
		   3) START-20

4.  ENTER THE DATE IN THE FOLLOWING MANNER: DATE MM/DD/YY
    WHERE MM IS THE MONTH, DD IS THE DAY, YY IS THE YEAR.
    I.E.  NOVEMBER 9,1974 WOULD BE ENTERED AS:

	 DATE 11/09/74

    THE CRT SCREEN SHOULD BE CLEARED AND ONE DOT DISPLAYED.
    NOTE: MANY PROGRAMS USE THE OS/8 DATE INFORMATION.
	  FALURE TO ENTER THE DATE MAY CAUSE THE PROGRAM
	  TO USE AN ERRONEOUS DATE.

5.  CONSULT WRITEUP FOR DETAILED PROGRAM STARTUP
    AND RUNNING PROCEDURE.
